NAME
    gcloud alpha fault-testing experiments affected-resources describe -
        describe an affected resource

SYNOPSIS
    gcloud alpha fault-testing experiments affected-resources describe
        (AFFECTED_RESOURCE : --experiment=EXPERIMENT --location=LOCATION)
        [GCLOUD_WIDE_FLAG ...]

DESCRIPTION
    (ALPHA) Describe an affected resource.

EXAMPLES
    To describe an affected resource test-affected-resource-id associated with
    experiment test-experiment-id in location asia-east1 run

    $ gcloud alpha fault-testing experiments affected-resources \        describe test-affected-resource-id \
        --experiment=test-experiment-id --location=asia-east1

POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
     AffectedResource resource - The resource name of the affected resource.
     Format:
     projects/{projectId}/locations/{location}/experiments/{experimentId}/affectedResources/{affectedResourceId}.
     The arguments in this group can be used to specify the attributes of this
     resource. (NOTE) Some attributes are not given arguments in this group but
     can be set in other ways.

     To set the project attribute:
      ◆ provide the argument affected_resource on the command line with a
        fully specified name;
      ◆ provide the argument --project on the command line;
      ◆ set the property core/project.

     This must be specified.

       AFFECTED_RESOURCE
          ID of the affectedResource or fully qualified identifier for the
          affectedResource.

          To set the affected_resource attribute:
          ▸ provide the argument affected_resource on the command line.

          This positional argument must be specified if any of the other
          arguments in this group are specified.

       --experiment=EXPERIMENT
          The experiment id of the affectedResource resource.

          To set the experiment attribute:
          ▸ provide the argument affected_resource on the command line with a
            fully specified name;
          ▸ provide the argument --experiment on the command line.

       --location=LOCATION
          The location id of the affectedResource resource.

          To set the location attribute:
          ▸ provide the argument affected_resource on the command line with a
            fully specified name;
          ▸ provide the argument --location on the command line.

